iterations.reply:
I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and the contract says that clause is its entire authority. Importing `http-client` would exceed the declared grant. The approval would need to be recorded in the graph's `with` clause, not added in the node body. The fetch would also send the raw reply text to an external host, which the contract doesn't account for.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The `requires` clause (len(text) <= 100000) holds of every input.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // `ensures` checks: a violating output is never returned. With
        // panic = "abort" these trap instead of returning bad data.
        assert!(confirmation.delivered, "ensures violated: delivered == true");
        assert!(!confirmation.session.is_empty(), "ensures violated: present(session_id)");

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

